@startuml Sequence_B_Failover
hide footbox
autonumber
actor User
participant "Bank Core" as Core
participant "Notification API" as API
database "PostgreSQL FSM" as DB
participant "Outbox Relay" as Relay
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Router" as Router
participant "Scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "Push Worker" as Push
participant "FCM / APNs" as FCM
participant "SMS Worker" as SMS
participant "SMS Provider" as SMSP
participant "Callback API" as Callback

Core -> API: POST critical event
API -> DB: Persist notification + outbox
DB --> API: COMMIT
API --> Core: 202 Accepted
Relay -> Kafka: Publish P0 event
Kafka -> Router: Consume
Router -> DB: Set PUSH_PENDING
Router -> Kafka: Publish push task (outbox)
Kafka -> Push: Consume
Push -> FCM: Submit push
FCM --> Push: Accepted (not device confirmation)
Push -> DB: Persist provider acceptance
Router -> DB: Set WAITING_FOR_APP_ACK; next_action_at = now + 8s
... due time reached; still no App ACK ...
Scheduler -> DB: SELECT due rows FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
DB --> Scheduler: notification_id + version
Scheduler -> DB: CAS WAITING_FOR_APP_ACK -> SMS_RESERVED
Scheduler -> DB: BEGIN; insert SMS task + outbox; COMMIT
Relay -> DB: Poll committed outbox row
Relay -> Kafka: Publish SMS task
Kafka -> SMS: Consume SMS task
SMS -> SMSP: Submit SMS
SMSP --> SMS: Accepted / provider reference
SMS -> DB: Save SMS attempt
SMSP -> Callback: DLR (when available)
Callback -> Kafka: Callback event
Kafka -> Router: Consume DLR
Router -> DB: Apply monotonic state transition
note over Router,DB
CAS/version prevents concurrent schedulers from
creating multiple SMS tasks for the same transition.
A provider timeout after acceptance remains UNKNOWN;
reconcile before another SMS submission.
end note
@enduml
